      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the number of ways 9 people can sit around a round table, we need to consider the circular permutations. In a circular permutation, we fix one person and arrange the remaining people in the remaining seats. This is because rotating the entire arrangement does not produce a new arrangement.\n\nFor $n$ people sitting around a round table, the number of distinct arrangements is given by $(n-1)!$.\n\nIn this problem, we have 9 people. So, the number of distinct ways to arrange them around the table is:\n\\[\n(9-1)! = 8! = 40320\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of ways 9 people can sit around a round table is \\(\\boxed{40320}\\).",
